      "severity": "major",
      "description": "The player evoked Solitude by exiling Atraxa, Grand Unifier — one of the most powerful cards in their hand — to remove an unknown target (likely nothing threatening on board since the opponent has no visible creatures). Atraxa is an extremely high-value card being pitched for minimal gain. Furthermore, Solitude's ETB exiles 'up to one other target creature,' but the opponent appears to have no creatures on the battlefield, making this evoke accomplish almost nothing while sacrificing a premium card. Even if there were a target, exiling Atraxa (a 7-mana bomb) to evoke Solitude on turn 3 when the opponent has no board presence is a terrible trade.",
