      "description": "Discarding Solitude during the beginning of turn 4 (before combat) to pump Psychic Frog with a +1/+1 counter. Solitude is an extremely powerful card that can be evoked to exile a creature by pitching a white card, and it serves as the only remaining card in hand. While pumping the Frog is valuable, discarding the last card in hand means GPT4om Vorthos is now hellbent with no interaction available. However, with all three lands tapped and Solitude requiring a white card to evoke (and no other white cards in hand), the Solitude was effectively dead for its evoke mode. The question is whether holding it for a future hard-cast (at 5 mana) or as a potential evoke target later (if a white card is drawn) would be more valuable than the +1/+1 counter now. Given the opponent has an empty board and no cards visible, the aggressive pump to make Frog a 2/3 (or 3/4 with prior counters) for combat damage + card draw is reasonable, but going hellbent sacrifices future flexibility.",
